{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","modules":[{"name":"AutomaticScreenTracking"}],"externalID":"AutomaticScreenTracking","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track a screen view each time a screen’s view controller appears, without a modifier or a call on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each screen."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this module when an app’s screens should track their own views: on iOS, iPadOS, tvOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"visionOS and Mac Catalyst through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIWindowScene","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and on macOS through an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSWindow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"watchOS and Linux it builds empty. To track one screen by hand, or a view a macOS","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NavigationStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pushes, give it ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is tracked until a window scene or a window turns it on with ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreensAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A screen is a view controller on screen none of whose children is: the one a navigation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"controller shows, a tab’s, one presented. It tracks ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once as it appears, and again","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when it reappears after being covered or hidden. The screen is named after its controller’s type,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or for a hosting controller after the type of the SwiftUI view it shows. The closure gets each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiscoveredScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and returns the event to track, renamed, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to skip the screen:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ In the scene delegate's scene(_:willConnectTo:options:), beside the scene's tracker:","windowScene.traitOverrides.tracker = tracker","windowScene.trackScreensAutomatically { screen in","    screen.name == \"DebugMenuViewController\" ? nil : ScreenViewed(screen: screen.name)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On macOS, a window turns it on, and each screen view goes through the tracker the screen’s view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finds up its responder chain ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSView.tracker"},{"type":"text","text":", from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import AppKit","import SwiftUI","","struct PreferencesView: View {","    var body: some View {","        Text(\"Preferences\")","    }","}","","final class PreferencesWindowController: NSWindowController, TrackerProviding {","    let tracker: Tracker","","    init(tracker: Tracker) {","        self.tracker = tracker","        super.init(window: NSWindow(contentViewController: NSHostingController(rootView: PreferencesView())))","    }","","    required init?(coder: NSCoder) { nil }","}","","let controller = PreferencesWindowController(tracker: tracker)","controller.window?.trackScreensAutomatically()  \/\/ tracks ScreenViewed(screen: \"PreferencesView\")","controller.showWindow(nil)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"kinds:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" limits tracking to UIKit’s (or AppKit’s) view controllers or to SwiftUI’s views. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI screen given ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left to that modifier, so it isn’t tracked twice.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Discovery looks after each turn of the main run loop, swizzles nothing, and touches no other scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or window. On a UIKit platform, each screen view goes through the tracker the screen’s traits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hold, so each scene keeps its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This documentation is built on macOS, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIWindowScene","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreensAutomatically(kinds:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"stopTrackingScreensAutomatically()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" have no pages here; they take the same parameters as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSWindow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s, with ","type":"text"},{"code":"kinds:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" defaulting to ","type":"text"},{"code":"[.uiKit, .swiftUI]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and their doc comments are in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sources.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"also covers control activations and the app’s lifecycle.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"API","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"API"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s API isn’t there, so its symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for an Apple target.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Tracking-a-windows-screens","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Tracking a window’s screens"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSWindow.trackScreensAutomatically(kinds:_:)"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NSWindow.stopTrackingScreensAutomatically()","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Naming-screens","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Naming screens"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DiscoveredScreen","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DiscoveredScreen.Kind","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking"]}],"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/appkittracking":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppKitTracking"}],"title":"AppKitTracking","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","type":"link"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.i